# Git branch and push workflow

- Never push commits directly to `main`.
- For every set of changes to ship: create a new feature branch (e.g. `feature/T-###-short-name`).
- Push the feature branch and merge it into `dev` (PR into `dev`, or merge locally then push `dev`).
- Do not merge to `main` unless the user explicitly asks for a release/promote.
